Z||000020||Patrick's Dad||04-02-2000||09:47 PM||||Formula, I read that as Domestics only are limited to four cylinders. Foreign subcompacts can have sixes, as long as a six (not necessarily the same six) is offerred as OEM option. The Dodge Stealth is allowed as a six, because it's made by Mitsubishi. It also seems that Volkwagen is the only approved German marque. This would mean bugs, Jettas, Corrados, Scirroccos, etc. No Audis, Porsches, or BMW (Many of which can run 200 without modification). It seems also to exclude Koreans [200 in an Excel??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ].<P>That's why, if I had the $$, I'd love to be the first to do it, and do it in a Fiero.<P>[This message has been edited by Patrick's Dad (edited 04-02-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Patrick's Dad (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||1
